My caveman had just cleared Ludious and was lugging a big
pile of loot out when much to my dismay a big purple L
appeared next to him and cast a spell. This was an XL 14
character and Ludious was entered from DL 11 if that makes
any difference. I hadn't seen anything remotely this
dangerous all the way down to DL 21.

Must be a shape changer, right? Still, what to do, I'll
still be just as dead if the shape changer uses the touch of
death while in the form of an arch-lich (No MR). I had a
/oTeleport and a /oCancellation but didn't know which was
which. The /oDig isn't going to make a hole in the floor at
Ludious, I wouldn't think.

My caveman was wearing jumping boots but I didn't see how I
could get away, the portal was way to far away. No ?oGen or
!oH. Finally I just settled for engraving Elbereth with the
/oDig. I wasn't absolutely sure that would stop it from
using the touch of death since Elbereth won't prevent ranged
attacks, including spells. I was hoping it could only use an
attack spell if it moved away and then it couldn't use the
touch of death.

I just kept hitting "." and the lich kept casting a spell
that made monsters aware of my presence, then it finally
turned into a dresser and, with a sigh of relief, I beat it
to death. Whew.
